    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a high-leverage slate today, with **Andy Pages** emerging as our strongest play at 71.21. Facing Kochanowicz and his inflated 5.12 xERA, **Andy Pages** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill projection, positioning him for a breakout day despite the minor drag of a high-percentage hold pitcher. Close behind is **Gunnar Henderson** (64.41), who remains a must-start not just for his elite pedigree, but because the matchup against Fisher offers a strategic opportunity to capitalize on a slow delivery, providing a 2% boost to his already high stolen base potential. **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) also draws a strong grade, bolstered by favorable winds and an ideal leadoff spot against Painter, which maximizes his 0.379 xwOBA potential.\n\nWe faced a difficult optimization choice regarding **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 43.55. While **Brayan Rocchio** maintains a respectable efficiency, he was ultimately benched in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Jackson Merrill**, as his projected spot at the bottom of the order significantly cannibalized his total output. We are closely monitoring the bottom of our lineup, particularly **Dominic Smith** (42.18); while he scrapes above the bench threshold, he faces a tough assignment against Ashcraft. His start is defensive in nature to preserve our game caps, though he remains a high-risk candidate if his early plate appearances suggest a lack of rhythm.\n\nRisk management is paramount today as we navigate matchups against several elite arms. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.69) faces a stiff challenge in Bradish, and while his order placement at #3 provides a cushion, his score is depressed by the SP skill factor. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** and **Miguel Vargas** must contend with an elite catcher\u2019s pop time against Painter, resulting in a slight efficiency penalty. With **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, but the configuration of our active roster prioritizes current wind conditions and the aforementioned platoon advantages to stay competitive in the scarcity-heavy stolen base category.",
